e maximizes immediate material gain and tempo.\n\nEvaluation: \n- **P: e6-d7**: Wins a rook with check, exploiting Black's king exposure. Material advantage (5-1) and initiative.\n- **P: e6-e7**: Quietly advances but allows Black's rook to capture it next turn (Rd7xe7), negating progress.\n- **Q: d1-g4**: Develops queen but misses the tactical opportunity; Black can respond with ...Rd7-d5 to defend.\n- **B: c6-d7**: Wins rook but trades bishop for rook (net +2), inferior to pawn capture (net +4).\n\nReason: Capturing the rook with check is the highest-impact move, combining material gain, tempo, and positional dominance. Delaying this capture risks Black repositioning the rook or defending the square.\n\nAnswer: P: e6-d7"}
